[{"id": "R025", "text": "I tap the borrowed tool, leave it, and plan to return it later. I try to open it, first finding the wrench still there and then finding the item already moving."}, {"id": "R026", "text": "I place the borrowed tool on the bench and keep both people near it. I move the item once by hand, leave it, and if they continue disagreeing, I keep the tool and leave the item alone."}, {"id": "R027", "text": "I place the tool beside a broken wheel while the two people disagree about who should move first. I rub rust from the wheel, take the tool, leave the wheel on the bench, and pocket the broken bolt."}, {"id": "R028", "text": "I put the tool down, stay with the hand holding the item, and ask who moved it, using the hand's position as evidence. If the answer is that it was put down again, I leave the hand with the item and keep the tool in the queue."}, {"id": "R029", "text": "I tap the old tool twice and keep it beside the bench, then tap an old nail on the wall and leave a new one beside it. I keep my hand near the old nail, tap it once, leave the old tool beside the bench, and leave the nail bent and rusted."}, {"id": "R030", "text": "I hold the tool near the disagreement, tap it with my thumbnail, and tell one person to move the old one first before placing it beside the new one. I leave the old one against the wall, watch the other person pick it up and touch its edge with a pencil, then leave the tool alone and wait for the disagreement to change."}, {"id": "R031", "text": "I hold the tool against my chest and tap a page edge twice while the people indicate different hands. I move the scrap toward the back, place it beside the tool, tap the paper once, and leave the scrap beside the tool."}, {"id": "R032", "text": "I move toward the tool and touch its handle, then stop when the other person does not move it and put it down. I place the other person's hand on the tool, note that the tool is not in my hand, leave it there, check the other person's hand, and then stop."}, {"id": "R033", "text": "I keep the tool aside, ask the borrower who moved it, and mark the tool's edge before leaving it behind. I plan to use the borrowed tool for one test and return it once the other person has settled."}, {"id": "R034", "text": "I put the tool down and watch the two hands, with one moving. I return the tool to the bench, put the piece the other person holds back on the shelf, and leave the disagreement unresolved."}, {"id": "R035", "text": "I place the tool beside the other one and stop while the people identify a hand and a watch. I express uncertainty, then check the dust pile and the watch."}, {"id": "R036", "text": "I hold out the tool and claim to have moved the thumb, but knock the item over once. After the other person claims to have moved the index and says the thumb stays, I imitate their voice and put the tool back in my pocket."}]
